    1. Test retry tooling does not exist in this reactor. No rerun count setting appears in any of
       the 145 POMs and no retry plugin is declared anywhere, so a baseline failure is real and
       reproducible and failing fast is safe. A reviewer who searches for the word retry will
       instead find a Spring retry APPLICATION library: a version property in the root aggregator,
       a managed entry, and three consuming child modules, with nothing whatsoever to do with test
       reruns.
    2. Coverage exclusions are not test exclusions. The root aggregator configures the coverage
       plugin with eight package glob exclusions, which remove those packages from coverage
       MEASUREMENT only. No test is disabled by them, and none of the eight matches this module's
       package. Relatedly and bindingly: the coverage agent execution declares an output data file
       but no property name, so it communicates with the test runner through the default argument
       line property export. A unit test runner declaration that set a literal argument line
       element would silently sever instrumentation and leave the coverage check goal evaluating an
       empty data set against its minimum line coverage ratio, reporting a false pass.
       Instrumentation must be verifiably live.
  -->
